{
  "dom_id": "step-q81351",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Which of the following statements are logically equivalent?\n\n- $X∧¬Y$\n- $¬(Y∨¬X)$\n- $¬Y∧(X∨X)$",
  "worked_solution": "Two statements are logically equivalent if they have the same truth table. So, we construct a truth table for the three given statements:\n\n| $\\,X\\,$ | $\\,Y\\,$ | $\\,X∧¬Y\\,$ | $\\,¬(Y∨¬X)\\,$ | $\\,¬Y∧(X∨X)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nWe see that all three statements have the same truth table, so they are logically equivalent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"",
